// asm functions are emitted *before* the ordinary definitions, so a call to
// one is already declared by the time it is used. Their signatures are not in
// the forward-declaration block, which only walks the program list -- and
// ordering is cheaper than threading the target triple through it.
emit_asm_then_main(string triple) {
  emit_asm_all(triple);
  def_all();
} return void;

asm_error(string name, string triple) {
  string asm_triples_v = asm_triples(name);
  print("error: no 'asm' definition of '" + name + "' for target '" + triple + "'; defined for: " + asm_triples_v);
} return void;
